      "message": "If drp_state is TOGGLE_ON, we should act as DRP, and as type-c spec says: \n4.5.2.2.3.2  Exiting from Unattached.SNK State \nA DRP shall transition to Unattached.SRC within tDRPTransition after the state of both CC pins is SNK.Open for tDRP − dcSRC.DRP ∙ tDRP, or if directed.\n\n4.5.2.2.7.2  Exiting from Unattached.SRC State \nA DRP shall transition to Unattached.SNK within tDRPTransition after dcSRC.DRP ∙ tDRP, or if directed. \n\nSo (the not support dual role auto toggle mode TCPC \u0026\u0026 PD_DRP_TOGGLE_ON of drp_state) should keep toggling within tDRPTransition even when cc is open.\n\nIf we want to go to LPM when drp_state is PD_DRP_TOGGLE_ON and cc is open, then we need to implement dual role auto toggle mode base on current TCPMv2 code. ",
